Dear all,

I am trying to create a function to add a combo box to a web page and
pass the field selected to R, and another function to enable the user
to pass an array to R, but both fail -at least: they dont totally
succeed.
I am putting my code at the bottom of this email, but here is what
happens:
For the combo box: my code generates a web page containing a combo box
with the two values "a" and "b", just as I wanted. But when I click on
the "submit" button, NA is printed on the webpage instead of "a" or
"b". it seems the variable 'listNames' is lost somehow. Nothing
changes if I assign listNames as a global variable.

For the array of inputs: the value entered by the user are simply not
taken into account.

I would be grateful if someone could have a look. Otherwise, the Rook
package was simply failing with RStudio and sometimes it crashes my R
session - I am running R from Eclipse using StatET. Maybe there is
some compatibility problem with the rJava package.

Cheers,
Sam

Here is the code. There shouldnt be any dependancies so one could
simply copy/paste it into R.

#for the combo box:

generateComboBox<-function(values,texts,which.selected=1,variable)
{
	res<-'<form method=GET><div>\n'
	res<-paste(res,'<select name="',variable,'">\n',sep='')
	nChoices<-length(values)
	for(i in 1:nChoices)
	{
		tmp<-paste('<option
value="',values[i],'"',ifelse(i==which.selected,'
selected',''),'>','',texts[i],'</option>\n',sep='')
		res<-paste(res,tmp,sep='')
	}
	res<-paste(res,'</select>\n')
	res<-paste(res,'<div><input type="submit" value="submit"></
div>',sep='')
	res<-paste(res,'</form>')
	return(res)
}

testComboBox<-function(env)
{
	num<-1
	listNames<-c("a","b")
	req <- Rook::Request$new(env)
	res <- Rook::Response$new()

	if (!is.null(req$GET()[['num']]))
		num <- req$GET()[['num']]
	res
$write(generateComboBox(1:2,listNames,which.selected=num,variable='num'))
	res$write(listNames[num])
	res$finish()
}

s<-Rhttpd$new()
#
#s$add(name='testPlot',app='appExample3.R')
s<-Rhttpd$new()
s$add(name='testComboBox',app=testComboBox)
s$start(quiet=TRUE)
s$print()
s$browse(1)

